# Fixed 2026-10-09, defect 524, lane b16-compiler (class adjacent).
# Symptom: a function head that failed over several lines held back the
# report that its body is missing, where the same head on one line was told
# both: `function f(a: i64,` over `        b: 5)` over no body was told the
# `5` alone, its missing body only once the `5` was a type.
# Cause: `parse/opening.body_follows` silenced the absent body of any failed
# head that crossed a line, since a head's recovery can read the body's own
# line inside its brackets (`function f(` over `    y = 3 )`). It now holds
# the report back only where the head went on to a line at its body's
# margin, one level below its own; at any other margin the lines are the
# head's, and its body is told missing as on one line.
# This case: the head over two lines, a list aligned under its first
# parameter, and a head that goes on at its body's margin, whose missing
# body is held back as before, its second line standing where a body would.

function two_lines(a: i64,
        b: 5)  #~ expected_type

function aligned(a: i64,  #~ missing_body
                 b: i64,
                 c: [5])  #~ expected_type

function held(a: i64,  #~ missing_body
    b: 5)  #~ expected_type

function main()
    print(1)
